Somewhat OT, but whatever:

lojbab:

> [...] it changes the nature of the underlying relationship/predication. 
>  To allow that would destroy one of the fundamental logical parts of the 
> language, which is that even if a place is elided, it is still implicitly a 
> part of the predication/relationship. 
>

Which has just reminded me of why the problem (nabmi be mi) of connecting 
predicates with JE bugs me so much. Usage seems to disregard all 
non-explicit places in that very common kind of construction. Provocatively 
speaking, if we uphold 'one of the fundamental logical parts of the 
languages', super-common stuff like CLL 12.12 {ti blanu je zdani} is 
nonsense.

Yes, I brought this up 
<https://groups.google.com/forum/#!msg/lojban-beginners/wZZu2LjksLE/JfcszCvyFKYJ> 
before 
<https://mw-live.lojban.org/papri/Talk:BPFK_Section:_Logical_Connectives>. 
